# WASM size baseline
#
# This file stores the reference size (in bytes) of the compiled contract WASM
# artifact. The CI `wasm-size` job compares the freshly built artifact against
# this baseline and fails when the contract grows past the budget.
#
# Format: a single integer (bytes) on the first non-comment, non-empty line.
# The value below is the budget limit (baseline + allowed headroom).
#
# To update after an intentional size change:
#   1. Build the contract: `cargo build --release --target wasm32-unknown-unknown`
#   2. Record the new artifact size in bytes.
#   3. Update the value below (optionally add a small headroom margin).
#
# Budget limit (bytes):
65536